WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.760
BHW Marites notices standing water in three yards. She speaks with residents and asks what they have noticed too.

2
00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:19.100
Marites invites residents, the purok leader, and health staff to talk. Someone suggests another time; she listens before they choose a time together.

3
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:29.960
Marites records what she saw: standing water in three yards. She does not claim it caused children to become ill, because that has not been established.

4
00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:41.820
With residents and health staff, she identifies who will bring the concern to the barangay planning team for health and who will report back. Confirm the actual route with the local health team.

5
00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:52.680
Barangay input may inform discussion for the Local Investment Plan for Health, or LIPH. It goes through the existing local process; funding is not guaranteed.

6
00:00:52.980 --> 00:01:05.900
As a Community Organizer, Marites listens, connects people, reports what was seen rather than assumed, and follows the local process until residents receive a response.
